# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets headers.
#
# IMPORTANT SCOPE: on Cloudflare, `_headers` applies ONLY to responses
# served from static assets. It is NOT applied to responses generated by
# the Worker (SSR pages, API routes, proxy responses) — those keep the
# headers set by `next.config.ts` `headers()` and `src/proxy.ts`
# (security headers + CSP), which the OpenNext adapter carries into the
# Worker. Do not move security headers or the CSP into this file; they
# would silently stop applying to dynamic responses.
#
# This file exists for the one thing it can actually govern: long-lived
# caching of hashed build assets (the same rule vercel.json expresses
# for Vercel; Cloudflare ignores vercel.json).
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
